  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-05T19:34:06.534Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In order to avoid tons of any state transitions, I'm currently working on an asset which builds a bunch of animator layers which each individually monitor a single input parameter, and fire off a parameter driver when that input changes. This is inefficient and can require dozens of always-running animator transitions and layers to detect what the VRChat client already knows. If the VRChat client could set an animator trigger when a parameter is changed due to action menu manipulation or network sync, I could eliminate the need for these trigger layers and greatly improve the performance of my animator.",
